WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.100
NICK: Wren...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.740
WREN: So I... I noticed that there was this little M&amp;M

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.920
peeking out of this trail mix bag,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.800
and I thought it was a dart-- a little Nerf dart.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.940
I was like, "Ah, there's a Nerf dart! Oh, it's just an M&amp;M."

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.040
And then Nick got to looking at it and he was like,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.200
"Why is there, like, a random little nibbled hole in this bag?"

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.200
So check this out:

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.220
what does this look like to you?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.820
I don't want to make any broad statements but we have so many rats right now.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.460
BEN: [shouting] What!?

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.120
NICK: We have rats, dude. Or mice.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.980
[Cut to clip from Scary Movie 3]
MAN 1: Rats are outside, mice are inside.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.200
MAN 2: Yo, but what if a mouse goes outside? Does it become a rat?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.980
And if a rat is in the house, is it a mouse?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.060
MAN 1: I ain't seen no mouse outside, that's what I'm sayin'.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.680
MAN 2: That's because it's a rat, fool!

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.400
BEN: No, that's just how Carmichael eats.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.880
WREN: For what it's worth, I've never seen any rodents here.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.040
We don't have any other evidence.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.080
BEN: Worst case scenario, how does this play out?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.120
We're all dead in 6 months, is what it means.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.040
NICK: Yeah.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.360
WREN: What do you think this is?

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.120
BRETT: It looks like bite marks, son.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.500
WREN: What do you think caused that hole?

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.460
SAM: Munchkins.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.460
NICK: So we're gonna set up a a time lapse

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.560
overnight and see if we can catch any

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.820
mice or rats or...

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:22.920
...Peters, or...

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.000
...whatever it may be.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.900
[Keyboard clicking]

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.660
NICK: There's 2,000 photos. It was going all night.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.020
Watch the M&amp;Ms... and they moved.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.460
That leads me to believe... Oh!

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.020
NICK: [gasps] Oh!
WREN: Oh, there it-- yeah! Wait, wait, wait, wait wait--

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.640
ALL: [exclaiming]

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.640
NICK: Dude!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.780
CARMICHAEL (?): There's a rat in the office!
BRETT: Shit, there is a rat, dude.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.820
NICK: He lives on my desk, dude? That's not sanitary! Holy shit!

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.400
WREN: You have a rat livin' on your desk, bro.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.680
NICK: Dude!
CARMICHAEL: Dude, he's huge!

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.540
CARMICHAEL: The rat is as big as this cup!

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.680
BRETT: [calmly] You were right, son. You were right.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.520
CARMICHAEL: What the hell are you dressed like that for!?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.160
BRETT: Dude, I am a goon, son.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.340
WREN: Oh my god, I can't believe it, dude.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.300
It... worked!

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:01.800
NICK: [laughter]

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.040
CARMICHAEL: Take a snapchat!

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.600
NICK: Does he live over here...?

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.400
CARMICHAEL: Does he climb up there...?

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.960
NICK: He makes multiple trips.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.240
WREN: You can see him eatin'!

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.340
NICK: Dude, he's pretty cute.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.180
Wren: Well, let's see if he, uhh... [tapping keys]

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.960
...ever comes back...

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.600
CARMICHAEL: D'you wanna see the rat?

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.080
NIKO: [laughter]
JAKE: You got it on timelapse!?

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.740
WREN: Yeah! We got it on camera, man!

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.500
JAKE: Oh, there it is.
NIKO: Whoa!

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.620
JAKE: [softly] our little fucker.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.620
NIKO: Look at that little cute guy.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.580
NIKO: Why was Nick recording a timelapse of the corner of his desk?

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.800
WREN: To... To catch the... the rat.
JAKE: To catch the rat.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.480
JAKE: Let's-- we need to put a bounty on its head.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.260
What, 20 bucks?

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.100
NIKO: [eating] I decree that whoever catches the rat...

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.800
...shall get a 6-pack of any beer of their choice!

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.780
CARMICHAEL: [laughter]
JAKE: Alright, deal.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.400
CARMICHAEL:

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.120
SAM: You're gonna lead me into a dark room.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.820
Is this a trick?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.540
SAM: I have no idea what this is.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.020
This is just an ambush.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.040
[Paper crinkling]

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:00.760
SAM: Wow.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.720
Son of a bitch.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.600
SPENCER: It's-- it's tiles and terrain.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.360
This is the modular stuff, so it's actually super awesome.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.660
It's the city-builder stuff.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.400
SAM: All their previous sets came in just, kind of-- just general squares.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.640
You'd just slide them together.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.360
But their latest set comes with

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.260
very, very, very well-designed...

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.560
...basically, posts, as you can see here.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.920
These things plug into the walls here

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.800
and allow you to create structures

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.480
You can do multiple stories,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.220
You can do rooms...

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.600
SPENCER: So right here, it's drapes for the window.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.780
SAM: ...frickin' nerd. Frickin' got drapes.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.200
I would literally never buy real drapes.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.120
But I would get miniature drapes any day.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.140
SPENCER: [laughter]

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.960
SAM: Honestly, I'm just totally blown away.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.680
I wanna give a huge shout-out to Dwarven Forge.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.740
Thanks, guys, for, uh, getting us some of this gear,

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.940
and I cannot wait to start using this in videos.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.040
If you guys haven't checked out their site, do it now.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.960
They make the best stuff.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.220
NIKO: So we have a mouse living in our house.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.080
It's been chewed out here... There's a bunch of dust all over the...

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.420
...ground here from it.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.320
I happen to have... two very good mousetraps next door.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.660
They go by the names of Corri and Roto.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.600
NICK: Niko just alerted me that Jan is coming by.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.100
[Nerf gun clicking]

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.900
[Sounds of a pitched Nerf battle]

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.560
JAN: I could use some support!

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.860
JAN: Yes!

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.160
JAN: God--!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:41.700
Right in the knuckle!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:42.780
WREN: [laughter]

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.220
WOMAN: I'm getting good, I'm totally gonna win, and then he shot me in the face.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.420
JAN: [out of breath] Hi, guys, how's it going? [laughter]

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.100
NIKO: Ah, I got shot right in the neck.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.080
[imitates a bullet impact] Aah!

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.860
CARMICHAEL: Now, with the rat running around

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.980
and, now, Corri hunting it somewhere in the studio,

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.580
I figured I could make a rat trap.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.600
For this DIY rat trap, we're going to need a few things.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.600
This rod that I found.
[Rod clatters to the workbench]

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.340
Peanut butter.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.460
Nice little water bucket.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.980
This is gonna be my pilot hole.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.660
[Drill whirring]

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.220
[Hi there, Nick]

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.380
CARMICHAEL: Ta-da!

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.060
[Drill whirring]

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.140
CARMICHAEL: So, we're not gonna drown the rat.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.080
Instead, it's just gonna go... to the farm!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.860
Where our first two cats live...

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:21.980
...and all the Peters live...

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.020
[Dremel buzzing]

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.620
NICK: Hey, there we go.
CARMICHAEL: Yay!

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:30.260
NICK: We're ready to smear peanut butter all over this bottle.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.840
CARMICHAEL: Yep.
NICK: Do we have any peanut butter?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.360
CARMICHAEL: We do have peanut butter. It's right in front of you.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:35.700
NICK: Ayyyy.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.940
NICK: Aw, man. Why d'you gotta do that, man?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.760
You just got peanut butter everywhere.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.400
NICK: Don't-- dude, really, though?

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.020
No, you clean it up!

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.020
BEN: Oh, god!

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.980
CARMICHAEL: [laughter]
NICK: [exclaiming]

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.560
WREN: There was a fly in my wine I was drinkin' last night.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.300
I had to spit it out on the table.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.820
BEN: [haughty voice] While I was having a fine vintage, a...

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.240
NICK and CARMICHAEL: [laughter]

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.980
BEN: ...airborne insect made its way into my esophageal tract.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.520
WREN: I tounged it, man!

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.960
WREN: [imitating a dying fly]

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:15.520
NICK: Nothin'.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:16.800
NICK: Did you check it?

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.840
CARMICHAEL: Yeah. The time laps shows that he... wasn't even there

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.340
There's one last thing to do.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:22.840
Go to Amazon...

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.420
CARMICHAEL: I-- I hope this is the big one.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.260
NICK: So, Carmichael bought some rat traps, and we set 'em around, and it's been a couple days now, but...

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:31.520
...ehh, there's nothin'.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:34.040
We put out four of them: two upstairs, one here,

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.800
and then one in between me and Carmichael's desks where we found the rat.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.800
Niko thinks the rat has literally just left the studio since we took away all the food.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.040
Maybe we'll... we'll never catch him. That's probably for the best for all of us.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.580
[Rat squeaking]

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.640
[Squeaking continues]

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:58.980
[Sniffing]

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.660
[Romantic harp sound effect]

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.720
NICK: Carmichael, what happened?
CARMICHAEL: I got it!

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.360
NICK: Is it ali-- it's dead?
CARMICHAEL: It's so big!

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:25.480
WREN: He's, like, dead.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.100
NIKO: People might give us some crap for

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.380
using a lethal rat trap.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.760
Let's be honest. It's a rodent.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.320
They spread disease.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.040
They put poop everywhere.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.940
If they get into your food, they can make you very sick.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.460
Also, for what it's worth, it's a humane rat trap.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.820
Meaning, there are spikes and the bar, and when the bar closes on that rat,

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.480
it's going to instantly just break its spine,

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.360
and pretty much... [snaps] lights out instantly.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.480
[Rat trap snaps closed]

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:58.560
NIKO: Well, that... That's a pretty solid ident in that pencil.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.980
That's pretty much an instant guillotine for a rat.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.380
Now we have to clean it up! [laughter]

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.080
CARMICHAEL: You know what we should do now?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.480
Watch our favorite Disney movie, Ratatouille.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.000
NICK: That's not my favorite.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:10.680
NICK: Alright.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:11.500
CARMICHAEL: Lesson learned?

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:12.340
NIKO: Rat traps work.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.200
NICK: Confirmed.

